---
/**
 * What the privacy notice says about buying a licence: by pay button when
 * that is switched on in src/data/site.mjs, and by email either way.
 */
import { buying } from '../data/site.mjs';
---

{buying && (
  <Fragment>
    <p>
      <strong>By the pay button.</strong> The payment page is not part of this site. It is run by
      Stripe (Stripe Payments Europe, Limited, Ireland), and what you type there goes to Stripe.
      We never see your card or bank details.
    </p>
    <p>Stripe passes on to us what an invoice and a licence need:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name, your business name and the invoice address</li>
      <li>your email address, and your VAT ID if you gave one</li>
      <li>what you bought, what you paid and when</li>
      <li>your answer to "where did you hear of Biryar", if you gave one</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      More about what Stripe itself does with payment data is in{' '}
      <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
)}

<p>
  <strong>By email.</strong> If you write to us to buy a licence, we use what you send (your
  business name, the invoice address, your email address) to write the invoice and to send the
  licence.
</p>
<p>
  Either way, we use this data to send your invoice and your licence, to tell you before a licence
  ends, and to answer you. We keep invoices for as long as German tax law requires, and delete the
  rest when it is no longer needed. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, the contract with you,
  and Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR, our duty to keep accounts.
</p>
